# playpick cell: mode=clear spec=druid:restoration style=mash size=25
# difficulty=heroic view=820x1180,touch save=carried (behaves as fresh, #273 --
# carried never actually carries across separate playbot invocations because
# the dev-server port is derived from the process pid).
#
# A fresh/carried save only opens Bonegrinder 10-normal by default, so
# #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the whole chain up to 25-heroic before backing
# out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at the door (direction.md's 2026-09-26
# driver-lesson recipe), rather than landing on the invite's own single-fight
# "visiting" framing.
#
# What no session has done before: `mash` on a healer has only ever been read
# inside one room at a time before now (mode=walk toward crowns and toward
# whisper, both 10-normal, both stalled or wiped in/near THE VIGIL; mode=daily
# Confluence 10-normal, wiped at 68s). This is the first time a healer under
# `mash` gets a full evening (mode=clear) to actually try, and the first at
# 25-heroic. scripts/playbot.ts's `play` loop never sets `want` for `mash`, so
# the body never steers in a fight -- it only round-robins the action bar in
# place -- but README's "every heal aimed at whoever is furthest from full"
# means those round-robin presses should still land on whoever needs it most,
# unlike a dps's round-robin, which lands on the boss regardless of who is
# hurt. Corridor crossing itself is not a question here (scripts/playbot.ts's
# own `cross()` steers at the door/room-boss independently of style, already
# confirmed for `mash` twice at 10-normal); what is open is whether an
# unsteered but correctly-targeted healer carries a 25-heroic raid through
# multiple boss rooms the way idle/wander/flee healers already have on this
# line, or whether heroic's tighter numbers expose the lack of positioning
# the way heroic already has for a tank under dodge (nine deaths, 2026-09-26).
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:druid:restoration
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

evening mash 220 6
state
shot end
says
bill
